{"verdict": "reject", "reason": "The task fails in both initial states and never disables the password. `password: \"{{ ansible.builtin.sha512(password) }}\"` references an undefined `password` variable and a nonexistent `sha512` function, so templating errors out. The user module also rejects the unsupported parameters `login_shell`, `manage_home`, and `password_sha512`. Even if the task ran, it would set a new SHA-512 hash instead of locking the account (e.g., `password_lock: true` or password `'!'`/`'*'`), so the `service` password would not be disabled."}
